id=first-waiting-for-min
class=derivation
found=the review behind 1.1.16, 2026-10-11
fixed=1.1.16
test=test/25_first_waiting_for.sql
detail=lock_tree_wide().first_waiting_for was min(waiting_for), the alphabetically least lock
       description, which is "first" only when every waiter in the tree wants the same lock. It is
       now the lock the longest-waiting session wants. test/25 builds one root whose older waiter
       queues on the table that sorts last, so the reverted min() picks the wrong lock and the file
       fails.
